# Promising Stairs: "At the beginning of your upkeep, surveil 1. You win the game if there are eight or more different names among unlocked doors of
# Rooms you control." The four Rooms there are give exactly eight names, so Bot1 unlocks them one door at a time: Promising Stairs and Unholy Annex on
# turn 1 (Black Lotus, three Moxen), Bottomless Pool and Roaring Furnace on turn 3, Locker Room on turn 5, Ritual Chamber on turn 7 (six names), Steaming
# Sauna on turn 9 (seven) and, last, Central Elevator on turn 11 (eight). At each of the upkeeps of turns 3 to 11 the count is below eight and the game goes on,
# in particular at turn 11's with seven (an `>= 7` would win there); at turn 13's, with eight, Bot1 wins. Central Elevator is unlocked last because its search
# shuffles the library, and nothing it could find remains there. The surveil keeps the top card each time.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Central Elevator // Promising Stairs
Unholy Annex // Ritual Chamber
Bottomless Pool // Locker Room
Roaring Furnace // Steaming Sauna
Swamp
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x26

